# =============================================================================
# PART 4 · MUST REMAIN UNSET IN PRODUCTION
# =============================================================================
# These variables either:
#   (a) point at the stale legacy Supabase project (`msdonkkechxzgagyguoe`
#       per nexapp CLAUDE.md §8), OR
#   (b) are development-only shortcuts, OR
#   (c) are admin bypasses that must only be enabled under explicit
#       sealed authorisation.
#
# Important: merely omitting a variable does not guarantee it is absent at
# runtime — some platforms (Vercel, Fly, etc.) can inject env vars from
# project-level settings. Verify absence via a safe runtime check (D10)
# before claiming the production environment is clean.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4.1 · Legacy Supabase (stale · points at non-canonical project per CLAUDE.md §8)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All four MUST BE ABSENT in production. nexapp code uses only the
# NEX_SUPABASE_* / NEXT_PUBLIC_NEX_SUPABASE_* names declared in Part 1.1.

# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4.2 · Dev-only shortcuts (not safe in production)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each of these enables a development convenience that would be a security
# or correctness risk in production. All must be absent/false in prod.

# NEX_ALLOW_DEV_ADMIN=
# NEX_DEV_ROUTES=
# NEX_AGENT_INTERNET_FORCE_OFFLINE=
# NEX_AGENT_INTERNET_FORCE_ONLINE=
# NEX_LOCAL_ONLY=

# Local Postgres only (never set in production serverless)
# NEX_LOCALPG_USER=
# NEX_LOCALPG_PORT=
# NEX_LOCALPG_PASSWORD=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4.3 · Admin bypass tokens (set only under sealed authorisation)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These enable founder-mode / cross-DB-reconciler / family-safety-admin
# bypass surfaces. Must only be set with explicit documented authorisation
# AND with corresponding Supabase-side policy to accept the bypass.

# NEX_FOUNDER_MODE_PASSWORD=
# NEX_FOUNDER_MODE_SECRET=
# NEX_FOUNDER_MODE_TTL_SEC=
# NEX_FOUNDER_SUPABASE_USER_ID=

# Must stay false unless authorised:
# NEX_CROSS_DB_RECONCILER_ENABLED=
# NEX_CROSS_DB_RECONCILER_SIMULATE_ONLY=

# Admin-only reader token · high sensitivity · bearer:
# NEX_FAMILY_SAFETY_ID_ADMIN_READER_TOKEN=


# =============================================================================
# PART 5 · NOT CONFIGURED FOR PHASE 1 LAUNCH
# =============================================================================
# These subsystems have env vars in the source code but are Phase 2+
# workstreams. Do NOT advertise these features as available until the
# corresponding workstream delivers a verified end-to-end implementation.
#
# Setting these variables will not make the features work for users.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5.1 · Payments · NOT IMPLEMENTED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payment integration is NOT WIRED in the current codebase. See the Phase F
# finding in docs/doctrine/nex-global-launch-readiness-2026-10-14.md: zero
# consumer of `new Stripe(...)`, no checkout route, no webhook handler.
# The only Stripe reference in src/ is a safe-logging regex.
#
# No STRIPE_* env var is read anywhere. Setting one would have no effect.
#
# Packages must NOT be advertised as purchasable until payment integration
# is designed, implemented, tested, and separately authorised. This is
# release blocker B3 in the Phase F report.
#
# (Deliberately empty: no STRIPE_* variables listed here.)


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5.2 · Regional market activation · NOT CONFIGURED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10 currencies are defined in src/lib/nex-native/currencies.ts (IDR, GBP,
# USD, EUR, SGD, MYR, THB, PHP, VND, AUD) for seller pricing display.
# These do NOT configure a market as launch-ready. No per-market payment
# provider mapping, no tax config, no regional availability flag.
#
# Market activation is release blocker B6/B7 in the Phase F report.
# Setting any currency symbol does not advertise that market as supported.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5.3 · LLM providers · NOT REQUIRED for Phase 1 chat+themes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 chat is human-to-human; no LLM auto-reply is required.
# The /api/nex-native/chat/nex-reply route exists but is not part of the
# Phase 1 user-facing contract. Setting LLM provider keys will not enable
# a verified Phase 1 feature.
#
# If an LLM provider is needed for a specific Phase 2 feature, configure
# via a separate, explicitly-authorised change. Do not set these for Phase 1.
#
# (Deliberately empty: no provider keys listed here.)


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5.4 · Observability / alerting · REQUIRED for Stage 1.1 Option C
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The sealed messaging-safety plan (Stage 1.1 Option C) requires an
# observability path to alert on fail-closed / fail-open events. See
# docs/doctrine/nex-stage-1-1-verification-and-failopen-decision-2026-10-14.md.
#
# Choose ONE webhook destination; others must remain unset.

# ---- Option A · Slack webhook ----
# NEX_ALERTS_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# NEX_ALERTS_DISPATCH_ENABLED=
# NEX_ALERTS_MIN_SEVERITY=

# ---- Option B · generic webhook ----
# NEX_ALERTS_WEBHOOK_URL=
# NEX_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=   # alternate legacy name
# NEX_ALERT_DEDUP_MS=
# NEX_ALERT_EMISSION=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5.5 · Other legacy src/lib/nex/* subsystems
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Author Studio, brain / agent / lab / programmer / workforce runtime,
# vision / image generation, OCR, voice, perceptual hashing, idempotency
# data roots, WhatsApp OTP, Twilio SMS, S3 / R2 / MinIO object storage
# alternatives, legacy marketing, legacy member tokens.
#
# All ~266 of these are documented in the B1 inventory §Section B rollup.
# They are NOT configured for Phase 1 launch. Code paths that touch them
# must degrade gracefully when the env is unset.
#
# Setting any of these does not enable a Phase 1 user-facing feature.
# Leave all unset for a Phase 1 production deployment unless a specific,
# authorised code path requires them.


